/.freebuff
/brag-output/

# Nothing is installed any more — there is no build step and no dependency — but
# a stray install would still never belong in the repo.
/node_modules

# Local secrets. A key in here is what lets the functions be exercised by hand
# (`wrangler dev` reads .dev.vars; .env is what a local runner reads), so the
# file has to exist — and it must never be committable, or the first
# `git add -A` publishes it.
/.env
/.env.local

# Local state from the old Netlify CLI, kept ignored in case one ever runs here
# again; .wrangler/ below is the tool that does now.
.netlify

# Local secret file for wrangler dev, same rule as .env above.
/.dev.vars

# Local Cloudflare tool state (local D1/cache, dev-server state) — never
# committed.
/.wrangler/

# Deploy staging output, written by tools/deploy-pages.mjs. Build output; also
# listed in .assetsignore, so it can never be uploaded even by hand.
/.pages-dist/
